    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80">

                <pb facs="0121" n="109" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.74/264: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-03-03T16:00:00-03:00">March 3, 1942—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:51 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>669. Department’s airmail instruction 2243, February 24 and telegram 525 March 2,
                        midnight.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d80-f1"/> The Minister of Communications
                    informed the Embassy that he would issue instructions today closing all
                    radio-telephone and radio-telegraph communication between Brazil and the Axis
                    nations et cetera, in compliance with Resolution XL of the Rio de Janeiro
                        Conference.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d80-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d80-f1" n="8" xml:id="d80-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d80-f2" n="9" xml:id="d80-f2-content">
                <p>For correspondence on the Third Meeting of the Foreign Ministers of the American
                    Republics at Rio de Janeiro, see <ref target="#pg6">pp. 6</ref> ff.; for text of
                    Resolution XL, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>,
                    February 7, 1942, p. 140.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
